{title: The First Noel}
{artist: Traditional English carol}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Carol}
{key: D}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}
{score: the-first-noel.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [D]first No[G]el the [D]angel did [A]say
Was to [D]certain poor [G]shepherds in [D]fields as they [A]lay
In [Bm]fields where they [A]lay keeping their [D]sheep
On a [G]cold winter's [D]night that was [A]so [D]deep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No[D]el, No[G]el, No[D]el, No[A]el
Born is the [D]King of Is[G]rael[A][D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They [D]looked up and [G]saw a [D]star
Shining [A]in the east be[D]yond them far
And [Bm]to the earth it [A]gave great [D]light
And [G]so it con[D]tinued [A]both day and [D]night
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
And [D]by the light of [G]that same [D]star
Three [A]wise men came from [D]country far
To [Bm]seek for a [A]king was their in[D]tent
And to [G]follow the [D]star wher[A]ever it [D]went
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
This [D]star drew nigh to the [G]north-west
O'er [D]Bethlehem it took its [A]rest
And [Bm]there it did [A]both stop and [D]stay
Right [G]over the [D]place where [A]Jesus [D]lay
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Then [D]entered in those [G]wise men [D]three
Full [A]reverently upon their [D]knee
And [Bm]offered there in His [A]presence
Their [G]gold and [D]myrrh and [A]frankin[D]cense
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Then [D]let us all with [G]one ac[D]cord
Sing [A]praises to our heavenly [D]Lord
That [Bm]hath made heaven and [A]earth of [D]naught
And [G]with His [D]blood man[A]kind hath [D]bought
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
